body:
{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {

  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {

  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {

  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The initials GPT stand for Generative Pretrained Transformer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5220,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that first word is straightforward enough, these are bots that generate new text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9800,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretrained refers to how the model went through a process of learning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13181,
    "dDurationMs": 3429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a massive amount of data, and the prefix insinuates that there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16610,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more room to fine-tune it on specific tasks with additional training."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20720,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the last word, that's the real key piece."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23380,
    "dDurationMs": 4191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A transformer is a specific kind of neural network, a machine learning model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27571,
    "dDurationMs": 3429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's the core invention underlying the current boom in AI."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31740,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I want to do with this video and the following chapters is go through a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35430,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "visually-driven explanation for what actually happens inside a transformer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39700,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're going to follow the data that flows through it and go step by step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43440,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are many different kinds of models that you can build using transformers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some models take in audio and produce a transcript."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51340,
    "dDurationMs": 2843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This sentence comes from a model going the other way around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54183,
    "dDurationMs": 2037,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing synthetic speech just from text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56660,
    "dDurationMs": 4402,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All those tools that took the world by storm in 2022 like DALL-E and Midjourney"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61062,
    "dDurationMs": 4458,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that take in a text description and produce an image are based on transformers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66000,
    "dDurationMs": 3737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if I can't quite get it to understand what a pi creature is supposed to be,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69737,
    "dDurationMs": 3363,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm still blown away that this kind of thing is even remotely possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73900,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the original transformer introduced in 2017 by Google was invented for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78000,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the specific use case of translating text from one language into another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82660,
    "dDurationMs": 3735,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the variant that you and I will focus on, which is the type that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86395,
    "dDurationMs": 4889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underlies tools like ChatGPT, will be a model that's trained to take in a piece of text,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91284,
    "dDurationMs": 3625,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe even with some surrounding images or sound accompanying it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94909,
    "dDurationMs": 3351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and produce a prediction for what comes next in the passage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98600,
    "dDurationMs": 2737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That prediction takes the form of a probability distribution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101337,
    "dDurationMs": 2463,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over many different chunks of text that might follow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105040,
    "dDurationMs": 2511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first glance, you might think that predicting the next word"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107551,
    "dDurationMs": 2389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "feels like a very different goal from generating new text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110180,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once you have a prediction model like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112519,
    "dDurationMs": 3683,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a simple thing you could try to make it generate, a longer piece of text,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116202,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to give it an initial snippet to work with,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118541,
    "dDurationMs": 3484,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have it take a random sample from the distribution it just generated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122025,
    "dDurationMs": 3832,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "append that sample to the text, and then run the whole process again to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125857,
    "dDurationMs": 3683,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a new prediction based on all the new text, including what it just added."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130100,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know about you, but it really doesn't feel like this should actually work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133420,
    "dDurationMs": 4526,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this animation, for example, I'm running GPT-2 on my laptop and having it repeatedly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137946,
    "dDurationMs": 4474,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predict and sample the next chunk of text to generate a story based on the seed text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142420,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The story just doesn't actually really make that much sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146500,
    "dDurationMs": 4793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if I swap it out for API calls to GPT-3 instead, which is the same basic model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151293,
    "dDurationMs": 4158,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just much bigger, suddenly almost magically we do get a sensible story,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155451,
    "dDurationMs": 4678,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one that even seems to infer that a pi creature would live in a land of math and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160129,
    "dDurationMs": 751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "computation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161580,
    "dDurationMs": 3351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This process here of repeated prediction and sampling is essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164931,
    "dDurationMs": 2415,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what's happening when you interact with ChatGPT,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167346,
    "dDurationMs": 3548,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or any of these other large language models, and you see them producing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170894,
    "dDurationMs": 986,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one word at a time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172480,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, one feature that I would very much enjoy is the ability to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175850,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see the underlying distribution for each new word that it chooses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183820,
    "dDurationMs": 2438,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's kick things off with a very high level preview"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186258,
    "dDurationMs": 1922,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how data flows through a transformer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188640,
    "dDurationMs": 3324,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We will spend much more time motivating and interpreting and expanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191964,
    "dDurationMs": 2422,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the details of each step, but in broad strokes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194386,
    "dDurationMs": 4274,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when one of these chatbots generates a given word, here's what's going on under the hood."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, the input is broken up into a bunch of little pieces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202620,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These pieces are called tokens, and in the case of text these tend to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206220,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "words or little pieces of words or other common character combinations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210740,
    "dDurationMs": 3337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If images or sound are involved, then tokens could be little"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214077,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "patches of that image or little chunks of that sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217580,
    "dDurationMs": 4626,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each one of these tokens is then associated with a vector, meaning some list of numbers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222206,
    "dDurationMs": 3154,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is meant to somehow encode the meaning of that piece."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225880,
    "dDurationMs": 4209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you think of these vectors as giving coordinates in some very high dimensional space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230089,
    "dDurationMs": 2917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "words with similar meanings tend to land on vectors that are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233006,
    "dDurationMs": 1674,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "close to each other in that space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235280,
    "dDurationMs": 2907,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This sequence of vectors then passes through an operation that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238187,
    "dDurationMs": 3088,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known as an attention block, and this allows the vectors to talk to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241275,
    "dDurationMs": 3225,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each other and pass information back and forth to update their values."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244880,
    "dDurationMs": 3602,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the meaning of the word model in the phrase \"a machine learning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248482,
    "dDurationMs": 3318,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "model\" is different from its meaning in the phrase \"a fashion model\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252260,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The attention block is what's responsible for figuring out which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255510,
    "dDurationMs": 3911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "words in context are relevant to updating the meanings of which other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259421,
    "dDurationMs": 2539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how exactly those meanings should be updated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262500,
    "dDurationMs": 2592,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And again, whenever I use the word meaning, this is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265092,
    "dDurationMs": 2948,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow entirely encoded in the entries of those vectors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269180,
    "dDurationMs": 3096,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After that, these vectors pass through a different kind of operation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272276,
    "dDurationMs": 3142,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and depending on the source that you're reading this will be referred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275418,
    "dDurationMs": 2782,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to as a multi-layer perceptron or maybe a feed-forward layer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278580,
    "dDurationMs": 1915,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here the vectors don't talk to each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280495,
    "dDurationMs": 2165,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all go through the same operation in parallel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283060,
    "dDurationMs": 2688,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while this block is a little bit harder to interpret,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285748,
    "dDurationMs": 3725,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "later on we'll talk about how the step is a little bit like asking a long list"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289473,
    "dDurationMs": 3584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of questions about each vector, and then updating them based on the answers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293057,
    "dDurationMs": 943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to those questions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294900,
    "dDurationMs": 3281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of the operations in both of these blocks look like a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298181,
    "dDurationMs": 3512,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giant pile of matrix multiplications, and our primary job is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301693,
    "dDurationMs": 3627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going to be to understand how to read the underlying matrices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306980,
    "dDurationMs": 3953,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm glossing over some details about some normalization steps that happen in between,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310933,
    "dDurationMs": 2047,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this is after all a high-level preview."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313680,
    "dDurationMs": 3557,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After that, the process essentially repeats, you go back and forth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317237,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between attention blocks and multi-layer perceptron blocks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320470,
    "dDurationMs": 3665,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until at the very end the hope is that all of the essential meaning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324135,
    "dDurationMs": 4365,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the passage has somehow been baked into the very last vector in the sequence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328920,
    "dDurationMs": 4405,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We then perform a certain operation on that last vector that produces a probability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333325,
    "dDurationMs": 4511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distribution over all possible tokens, all possible little chunks of text that might"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337836,
    "dDurationMs": 584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come next."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338980,
    "dDurationMs": 3338,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And like I said, once you have a tool that predicts what comes next"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342318,
    "dDurationMs": 3538,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given a snippet of text, you can feed it a little bit of seed text and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345856,
    "dDurationMs": 3238,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have it repeatedly play this game of predicting what comes next,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349094,
    "dDurationMs": 3986,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sampling from the distribution, appending it, and then repeating over and over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353640,
    "dDurationMs": 4304,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of you in the know may remember how long before ChatGPT came into the scene,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357944,
    "dDurationMs": 2498,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is what early demos of GPT-3 looked like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360442,
    "dDurationMs": 4198,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would have it autocomplete stories and essays based on an initial snippet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365580,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make a tool like this into a chatbot, the easiest starting point is to have a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369820,
    "dDurationMs": 4081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little bit of text that establishes the setting of a user interacting with a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373901,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "helpful AI assistant, what you would call the system prompt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377135,
    "dDurationMs": 4293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you would use the user's initial question or prompt as the first bit of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381428,
    "dDurationMs": 4293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dialogue, and then you have it start predicting what such a helpful AI assistant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385721,
    "dDurationMs": 1219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would say in response."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387720,
    "dDurationMs": 3254,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is more to say about an added step of training that's required"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390974,
    "dDurationMs": 2966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make this work well, but at a high level this is the idea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395720,
    "dDurationMs": 4244,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this chapter, you and I are going to expand on the details of what happens at the very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399964,
    "dDurationMs": 2765,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beginning of the network, at the very end of the network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402729,
    "dDurationMs": 3958,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I also want to spend a lot of time reviewing some important bits of background"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406687,
    "dDurationMs": 4244,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knowledge, things that would have been second nature to any machine learning engineer by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410931,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the time transformers came around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413060,
    "dDurationMs": 3157,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're comfortable with that background knowledge and a little impatient,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416217,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could probably feel free to skip to the next chapter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418626,
    "dDurationMs": 2036,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is going to focus on the attention blocks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420662,
    "dDurationMs": 2118,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "generally considered the heart of the transformer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423360,
    "dDurationMs": 3622,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After that, I want to talk more about these multi-layer perceptron blocks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426982,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how training works, and a number of other details that will have been skipped up to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431093,
    "dDurationMs": 587,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432180,
    "dDurationMs": 4026,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For broader context, these videos are additions to a mini-series about deep learning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436206,
    "dDurationMs": 2652,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's okay if you haven't watched the previous ones,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438858,
    "dDurationMs": 4073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think you can do it out of order, but before diving into transformers specifically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442931,
    "dDurationMs": 4073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I do think it's worth making sure that we're on the same page about the basic premise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447004,
    "dDurationMs": 1516,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and structure of deep learning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449020,
    "dDurationMs": 4228,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the risk of stating the obvious, this is one approach to machine learning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453248,
    "dDurationMs": 4558,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which describes any model where you're using data to somehow determine how a model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457806,
    "dDurationMs": 494,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behaves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459140,
    "dDurationMs": 3335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I mean by that is, let's say you want a function that takes in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462475,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an image and it produces a label describing it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464865,
    "dDurationMs": 3385,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or our example of predicting the next word given a passage of text,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468250,
    "dDurationMs": 3285,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or any other task that seems to require some element of intuition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471535,
    "dDurationMs": 1245,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pattern recognition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473200,
    "dDurationMs": 4495,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We almost take this for granted these days, but the idea with machine learning is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477695,
    "dDurationMs": 4443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than trying to explicitly define a procedure for how to do that task in code,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482138,
    "dDurationMs": 3397,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is what people would have done in the earliest days of AI,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485535,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead you set up a very flexible structure with tunable parameters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489194,
    "dDurationMs": 2718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a bunch of knobs and dials, and then, somehow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491912,
    "dDurationMs": 4443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you use many examples of what the output should look like for a given input to tweak"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496355,
    "dDurationMs": 3345,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tune the values of those parameters to mimic this behavior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499700,
    "dDurationMs": 4417,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, maybe the simplest form of machine learning is linear regression,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504117,
    "dDurationMs": 3114,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where your inputs and outputs are each single numbers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507231,
    "dDurationMs": 3397,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something like the square footage of a house and its price,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510628,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what you want is to find a line of best fit through this data, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514988,
    "dDurationMs": 1812,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to predict future house prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517440,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That line is described by two continuous parameters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520520,
    "dDurationMs": 3435,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say the slope and the y-intercept, and the goal of linear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523955,
    "dDurationMs": 4205,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regression is to determine those parameters to closely match the data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528880,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Needless to say, deep learning models get much more complicated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532620,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "GPT-3, for example, has not two, but 175 billion parameters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538120,
    "dDurationMs": 3832,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here's the thing, it's not a given that you can create some giant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541952,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "model with a huge number of parameters without it either grossly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545562,
    "dDurationMs": 3998,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overfitting the training data or being completely intractable to train."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550260,
    "dDurationMs": 2827,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Deep learning describes a class of models that in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553087,
    "dDurationMs": 3093,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "last couple decades have proven to scale remarkably well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556480,
    "dDurationMs": 3178,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What unifies them is that they all use the same training algorithm,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559658,
    "dDurationMs": 3321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's called backpropagation, we talked about it in previous chapters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562979,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the context that I want you to have as we go in is that in order for this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566679,
    "dDurationMs": 3795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "training algorithm to work well at scale, these models have to follow a certain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570474,
    "dDurationMs": 806,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specific format."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571800,
    "dDurationMs": 4251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you know this format going in, it helps to explain many of the choices for how a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576051,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transformer processes language, which otherwise run the risk of feeling kinda arbitrary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581440,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, whatever kind of model you're making, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583910,
    "dDurationMs": 2830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "input has to be formatted as an array of real numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586740,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This could simply mean a list of numbers, it could be a two-dimensional array,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590939,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or very often you deal with higher dimensional arrays,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593900,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the general term used is tensor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596560,
    "dDurationMs": 3957,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You often think of that input data as being progressively transformed into many"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600517,
    "dDurationMs": 3906,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distinct layers, where again, each layer is always structured as some kind of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604423,
    "dDurationMs": 4257,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "array of real numbers, until you get to a final layer which you consider the output."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609280,
    "dDurationMs": 4046,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the final layer in our text processing model is a list of numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613326,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "representing the probability distribution for all possible next tokens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617820,
    "dDurationMs": 4215,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In deep learning, these model parameters are almost always referred to as weights,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622035,
    "dDurationMs": 3958,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is because a key feature of these models is that the only way these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625993,
    "dDurationMs": 3907,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parameters interact with the data being processed is through weighted sums."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630340,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You also sprinkle some non-linear functions throughout,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632743,
    "dDurationMs": 1617,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they won't depend on parameters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635200,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Typically, though, instead of seeing the weighted sums all naked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638620,
    "dDurationMs": 3366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and written out explicitly like this, you'll instead find them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641986,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "packaged together as various components in a matrix vector product."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646740,
    "dDurationMs": 3676,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It amounts to saying the same thing, if you think back to how matrix vector"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650416,
    "dDurationMs": 3824,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multiplication works, each component in the output looks like a weighted sum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654780,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just often conceptually cleaner for you and me to think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658250,
    "dDurationMs": 3469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about matrices that are filled with tunable parameters that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661719,
    "dDurationMs": 3701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transform vectors that are drawn from the data being processed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666340,
    "dDurationMs": 3872,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, those 175 billion weights in GPT-3 are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670212,
    "dDurationMs": 3948,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "organized into just under 28,000 distinct matrices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674660,
    "dDurationMs": 2757,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those matrices in turn fall into eight different categories,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677417,
    "dDurationMs": 3813,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what you and I are going to do is step through each one of those categories to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681230,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understand what that type does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683160,
    "dDurationMs": 3927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we go through, I think it's kind of fun to reference the specific"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687087,
    "dDurationMs": 4273,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "numbers from GPT-3 to count up exactly where those 175 billion come from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691880,
    "dDurationMs": 2531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if nowadays there are bigger and better models,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694411,
    "dDurationMs": 2775,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this one has a certain charm as the first large-language"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697186,
    "dDurationMs": 3554,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "model to really capture the world's attention outside of ML communities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701440,
    "dDurationMs": 2737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, practically speaking, companies tend to keep much tighter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704177,
    "dDurationMs": 2563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lips around the specific numbers for more modern networks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707360,
    "dDurationMs": 3343,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I just want to set the scene going in, that as you peek under the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710703,
    "dDurationMs": 2726,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hood to see what happens inside a tool like ChatGPT,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713429,
    "dDurationMs": 4011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost all of the actual computation looks like matrix vector multiplication."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717900,
    "dDurationMs": 3983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a little bit of a risk getting lost in the sea of billions of numbers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721883,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you should draw a very sharp distinction in your mind between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725253,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the weights of the model, which I'll always color in blue or red,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728623,
    "dDurationMs": 3217,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the data being processed, which I'll always color in gray."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732180,
    "dDurationMs": 3978,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The weights are the actual brains, they are the things learned during training,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736158,
    "dDurationMs": 1762,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they determine how it behaves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738280,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The data being processed simply encodes whatever specific input is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742299,
    "dDurationMs": 4201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fed into the model for a given run, like an example snippet of text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747480,
    "dDurationMs": 4222,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With all of that as foundation, let's dig into the first step of this text processing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751702,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "example, which is to break up the input into little chunks and turn those chunks into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755973,
    "dDurationMs": 447,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vectors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757020,
    "dDurationMs": 2241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mentioned how those chunks are called tokens,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759261,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which might be pieces of words or punctuation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761501,
    "dDurationMs": 3385,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but every now and then in this chapter and especially in the next one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764886,
    "dDurationMs": 3194,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd like to just pretend that it's broken more cleanly into words."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768600,
    "dDurationMs": 2786,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because we humans think in words, this will just make it much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771386,
    "dDurationMs": 2694,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "easier to reference little examples and clarify each step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775260,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The model has a predefined vocabulary, some list of all possible words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779420,
    "dDurationMs": 3692,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say 50,000 of them, and the first matrix that we'll encounter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783112,
    "dDurationMs": 4688,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known as the embedding matrix, has a single column for each one of these words."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788940,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These columns are what determines what vector each word turns into in that first step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795100,
    "dDurationMs": 2975,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We label it W_E, and like all the matrices we see,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798075,
    "dDurationMs": 4285,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its values begin random, but they're going to be learned based on data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803620,
    "dDurationMs": 3758,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turning words into vectors was common practice in machine learning long before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807378,
    "dDurationMs": 3372,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transformers, but it's a little weird if you've never seen it before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810750,
    "dDurationMs": 2698,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it sets the foundation for everything that follows,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813448,
    "dDurationMs": 2312,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's take a moment to get familiar with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816040,
    "dDurationMs": 3871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We often call this embedding a word, which invites you to think of these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819911,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vectors very geometrically as points in some high dimensional space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824180,
    "dDurationMs": 3874,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Visualizing a list of three numbers as coordinates for points in 3D space would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828054,
    "dDurationMs": 3726,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be no problem, but word embeddings tend to be much much higher dimensional."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832280,
    "dDurationMs": 3656,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In GPT-3 they have 12,288 dimensions, and as you'll see,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835936,
    "dDurationMs": 4504,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it matters to work in a space that has a lot of distinct directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841180,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the same way that you could take a two-dimensional slice through a 3D space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845060,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and project all the points onto that slice, for the sake of animating word"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848791,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "embeddings that a simple model is giving me, I'm going to do an analogous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852471,
    "dDurationMs": 4278,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing by choosing a three-dimensional slice through this very high dimensional space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856749,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and projecting the word vectors down onto that and displaying the results."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861280,
    "dDurationMs": 4242,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The big idea here is that as a model tweaks and tunes its weights to determine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865522,
    "dDurationMs": 3208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how exactly words get embedded as vectors during training,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868730,
    "dDurationMs": 4296,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it tends to settle on a set of embeddings where directions in the space have a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873026,
    "dDurationMs": 1414,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kind of semantic meaning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874980,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the simple word-to-vector model I'm running here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877790,
    "dDurationMs": 4399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if I run a search for all the words whose embeddings are closest to that of tower,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882189,
    "dDurationMs": 3711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll notice how they all seem to give very similar tower-ish vibes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886340,
    "dDurationMs": 2441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want to pull up some Python and play along at home,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888781,
    "dDurationMs": 2599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is the specific model that I'm using to make the animations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891620,
    "dDurationMs": 2864,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not a transformer, but it's enough to illustrate the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894484,
    "dDurationMs": 3116,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "idea that directions in the space can carry semantic meaning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898300,
    "dDurationMs": 3887,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A very classic example of this is how if you take the difference between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902187,
    "dDurationMs": 3563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the vectors for woman and man, something you would visualize as a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905750,
    "dDurationMs": 4211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little vector in the space connecting the tip of one to the tip of the other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909961,
    "dDurationMs": 3239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's very similar to the difference between king and queen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915080,
    "dDurationMs": 3275,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's say you didn't know the word for a female monarch,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918355,
    "dDurationMs": 4052,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could find it by taking king, adding this woman minus man direction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922407,
    "dDurationMs": 3053,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and searching for the embedding closest to that point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927000,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least, kind of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928480,
    "dDurationMs": 3293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite this being a classic example for the model I'm playing with,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931773,
    "dDurationMs": 4164,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the true embedding of queen is actually a little farther off than this would suggest,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935937,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "presumably because the way queen is used in training data is not merely a feminine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939957,
    "dDurationMs": 823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "version of king."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941620,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I played around, family relations seemed to illustrate the idea much better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946340,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The point is, it looks like during training the model found it advantageous to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950461,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "choose embeddings such that one direction in this space encodes gender information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956800,
    "dDurationMs": 3281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another example is that if you take the embedding of Italy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960081,
    "dDurationMs": 4672,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you subtract the embedding of Germany, and add that to the embedding of Hitler,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964753,
    "dDurationMs": 3337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get something very close to the embedding of Mussolini."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968570,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's as if the model learned to associate some directions with Italian-ness,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973431,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and others with WWII axis leaders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976470,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe my favorite example in this vein is how in some models,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979931,
    "dDurationMs": 4256,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you take the difference between Germany and Japan, and add it to sushi,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984187,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you end up very close to bratwurst."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987350,
    "dDurationMs": 2837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also in playing this game of finding nearest neighbors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990187,
    "dDurationMs": 3663,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was very pleased to see how close cat was to both beast and monster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994690,
    "dDurationMs": 3053,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One bit of mathematical intuition that's helpful to have in mind,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997743,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially for the next chapter, is how the dot product of two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000703,
    "dDurationMs": 3147,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vectors can be thought of as a way to measure how well they align."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004870,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Computationally, dot products involve multiplying all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007693,
    "dDurationMs": 3418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corresponding components and then adding the results, which is good,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011111,
    "dDurationMs": 3219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since so much of our computation has to look like weighted sums."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015190,
    "dDurationMs": 4809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Geometrically, the dot product is positive when vectors point in similar directions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019999,
    "dDurationMs": 3607,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's zero if they're perpendicular, and it's negative whenever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023606,
    "dDurationMs": 2004,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they point in opposite directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026550,
    "dDurationMs": 3366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, let's say you were playing with this model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029916,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you hypothesize that the embedding of cats minus cat might represent a sort of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034906,
    "dDurationMs": 2104,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plurality direction in this space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037430,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To test this, I'm going to take this vector and compute its dot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040570,
    "dDurationMs": 2891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "product against the embeddings of certain singular nouns,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043461,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and compare it to the dot products with the corresponding plural nouns."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047270,
    "dDurationMs": 2949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you play around with this, you'll notice that the plural ones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050219,
    "dDurationMs": 3409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do indeed seem to consistently give higher values than the singular ones,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053628,
    "dDurationMs": 2442,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "indicating that they align more with this direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057070,
    "dDurationMs": 4546,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's also fun how if you take this dot product with the embeddings of the words one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061616,
    "dDurationMs": 2814,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two, three, and so on, they give increasing values,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064430,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's as if we can quantitatively measure how plural the model finds a given word."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070250,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, the specifics for how words get embedded is learned using data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074050,
    "dDurationMs": 3425,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This embedding matrix, whose columns tell us what happens to each word,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077475,
    "dDurationMs": 2075,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the first pile of weights in our model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080030,
    "dDurationMs": 4697,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using the GPT-3 numbers, the vocabulary size specifically is 50,257,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084727,
    "dDurationMs": 5043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and again, technically this consists not of words per se, but of tokens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090630,
    "dDurationMs": 3679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The embedding dimension is 12,288, and multiplying those"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094309,
    "dDurationMs": 3481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tells us this consists of about 617 million weights."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098250,
    "dDurationMs": 2376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go ahead and add this to a running tally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100626,
    "dDurationMs": 3184,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remembering that by the end we should count up to 175 billion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105430,
    "dDurationMs": 3326,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the case of transformers, you really want to think of the vectors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108756,
    "dDurationMs": 3374,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this embedding space as not merely representing individual words."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112550,
    "dDurationMs": 3963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For one thing, they also encode information about the position of that word,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116513,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we'll talk about later, but more importantly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119224,
    "dDurationMs": 3546,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should think of them as having the capacity to soak in context."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123350,
    "dDurationMs": 4058,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A vector that started its life as the embedding of the word king, for example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127408,
    "dDurationMs": 4005,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might progressively get tugged and pulled by various blocks in this network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131413,
    "dDurationMs": 4162,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that by the end it points in a much more specific and nuanced direction that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135575,
    "dDurationMs": 3017,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow encodes that it was a king who lived in Scotland,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138592,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and who had achieved his post after murdering the previous king,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141973,
    "dDurationMs": 2757,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and who's being described in Shakespearean language."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145210,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about your own understanding of a given word."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148250,
    "dDurationMs": 3477,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The meaning of that word is clearly informed by the surroundings,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151727,
    "dDurationMs": 3371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sometimes this includes context from a long distance away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155098,
    "dDurationMs": 4547,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so in putting together a model that has the ability to predict what word comes next,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159645,
    "dDurationMs": 3745,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the goal is to somehow empower it to incorporate context efficiently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164050,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To be clear, in that very first step, when you create the array of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167136,
    "dDurationMs": 3227,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vectors based on the input text, each one of those is simply plucked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170363,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the embedding matrix, so initially each one can only encode"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173496,
    "dDurationMs": 3274,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the meaning of a single word without any input from its surroundings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177710,
    "dDurationMs": 3852,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you should think of the primary goal of this network that it flows through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181562,
    "dDurationMs": 3852,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as being to enable each one of those vectors to soak up a meaning that's much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185414,
    "dDurationMs": 3556,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more rich and specific than what mere individual words could represent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189510,
    "dDurationMs": 3292,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The network can only process a fixed number of vectors at a time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192802,
    "dDurationMs": 1368,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known as its context size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194510,
    "dDurationMs": 3162,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For GPT-3 it was trained with a context size of 2048,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197672,
    "dDurationMs": 5131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the data flowing through the network always looks like this array of 2048 columns,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202803,
    "dDurationMs": 2207,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each of which has 12,000 dimensions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205590,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This context size limits how much text the transformer can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208657,
    "dDurationMs": 3173,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incorporate when it's making a prediction of the next word."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212370,
    "dDurationMs": 2672,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why long conversations with certain chatbots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215042,
    "dDurationMs": 3126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the early versions of ChatGPT, often gave the feeling of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218168,
    "dDurationMs": 3882,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bot kind of losing the thread of conversation as you continued too long."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223030,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'll go into the details of attention in due time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225230,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but skipping ahead I want to talk for a minute about what happens at the very end."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229450,
    "dDurationMs": 2541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember, the desired output is a probability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1231991,
    "dDurationMs": 2879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distribution over all tokens that might come next."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235170,
    "dDurationMs": 2589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if the very last word is Professor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237759,
    "dDurationMs": 2697,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the context includes words like Harry Potter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240456,
    "dDurationMs": 3075,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and immediately preceding we see least favorite teacher,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243531,
    "dDurationMs": 4154,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also if you give me some leeway by letting me pretend that tokens simply"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247685,
    "dDurationMs": 4207,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look like full words, then a well-trained network that had built up knowledge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251892,
    "dDurationMs": 3938,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Harry Potter would presumably assign a high number to the word Snape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256510,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This involves two different steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258310,
    "dDurationMs": 4742,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first one is to use another matrix that maps the very last vector in that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263052,
    "dDurationMs": 4558,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "context to a list of 50,000 values, one for each token in the vocabulary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268170,
    "dDurationMs": 4003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's a function that normalizes this into a probability distribution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272173,
    "dDurationMs": 3484,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's called softmax and we'll talk more about it in just a second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275657,
    "dDurationMs": 4211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but before that it might seem a little bit weird to only use this last embedding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279868,
    "dDurationMs": 4055,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make a prediction, when after all in that last step there are thousands of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283923,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other vectors in the layer just sitting there with their own context-rich meanings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1288930,
    "dDurationMs": 3747,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has to do with the fact that in the training process it turns out to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292677,
    "dDurationMs": 3747,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more efficient if you use each one of those vectors in the final layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296424,
    "dDurationMs": 3846,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to simultaneously make a prediction for what would come immediately after it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300970,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a lot more to be said about training later on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303240,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I just want to call that out right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305730,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This matrix is called the Unembedding matrix and we give it the label WU."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310210,
    "dDurationMs": 3364,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, like all the weight matrices we see, its entries begin at random,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313574,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they are learned during the training process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316470,
    "dDurationMs": 2977,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Keeping score on our total parameter count, this Unembedding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319447,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "matrix has one row for each word in the vocabulary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322028,
    "dDurationMs": 3622,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and each row has the same number of elements as the embedding dimension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1326410,
    "dDurationMs": 3971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's very similar to the embedding matrix, just with the order swapped,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330381,
    "dDurationMs": 3244,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it adds another 617 million parameters to the network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333625,
    "dDurationMs": 2964,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning our count so far is a little over a billion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336589,
    "dDurationMs": 3635,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a small but not wholly insignificant fraction of the 175 billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340224,
    "dDurationMs": 1566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll end up with in total."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342550,
    "dDurationMs": 2107,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the very last mini-lesson for this chapter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344657,
    "dDurationMs": 2244,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to talk more about this softmax function,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346901,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since it makes another appearance for us once we dive into the attention blocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351430,
    "dDurationMs": 5124,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea is that if you want a sequence of numbers to act as a probability distribution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356554,
    "dDurationMs": 2854,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say a distribution over all possible next words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1359408,
    "dDurationMs": 5182,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then each value has to be between 0 and 1, and you also need all of them to add up to 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365250,
    "dDurationMs": 4642,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, if you're playing the deep learning game where everything you do looks like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1369892,
    "dDurationMs": 4918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "matrix-vector multiplication, the outputs you get by default don't abide by this at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375330,
    "dDurationMs": 2455,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The values are often negative, or much bigger than 1,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377785,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they almost certainly don't add up to 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380510,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Softmax is the standard way to turn an arbitrary list of numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1384030,
    "dDurationMs": 4675,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a valid distribution in such a way that the largest values end up closest to 1,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388705,
    "dDurationMs": 2585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the smaller values end up very close to 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391830,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's all you really need to know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1393090,
    "dDurationMs": 4039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you're curious, the way it works is to first raise e to the power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397129,
    "dDurationMs": 4263,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of each of the numbers, which means you now have a list of positive values,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401392,
    "dDurationMs": 4207,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you can take the sum of all those positive values and divide each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1405599,
    "dDurationMs": 3871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "term by that sum, which normalizes it into a list that adds up to 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1410170,
    "dDurationMs": 4116,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll notice that if one of the numbers in the input is meaningfully bigger than the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1414286,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest, then in the output the corresponding term dominates the distribution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417966,
    "dDurationMs": 4165,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you were sampling from it you'd almost certainly just be picking the maximizing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422131,
    "dDurationMs": 339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "input."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422990,
    "dDurationMs": 4008,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's softer than just picking the max in the sense that when other values"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426998,
    "dDurationMs": 3852,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are similarly large, they also get meaningful weight in the distribution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1430850,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and everything changes continuously as you continuously vary the inputs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435130,
    "dDurationMs": 4854,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In some situations, like when ChatGPT is using this distribution to create a next word,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439984,
    "dDurationMs": 4686,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's room for a little bit of extra fun by adding a little extra spice into this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444670,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "function, with a constant T thrown into the denominator of those exponents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449550,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We call it the temperature, since it vaguely resembles the role of temperature in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1454000,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "certain thermodynamics equations, and the effect is that when T is larger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458121,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you give more weight to the lower values, meaning the distribution is a little bit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462681,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more uniform, and if T is smaller, then the bigger values will dominate more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1466911,
    "dDurationMs": 4615,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aggressively, where in the extreme, setting T equal to zero means all of the weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471526,
    "dDurationMs": 1264,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes to maximum value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473470,
    "dDurationMs": 4192,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, I'll have GPT-3 generate a story with the seed text,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1477662,
    "dDurationMs": 5288,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"once upon a time there was A\", but I'll use different temperatures in each case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483630,
    "dDurationMs": 4653,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Temperature zero means that it always goes with the most predictable word,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1488283,
    "dDurationMs": 4087,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what you get ends up being a trite derivative of Goldilocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1493010,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A higher temperature gives it a chance to choose less likely words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496540,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it comes with a risk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498230,
    "dDurationMs": 2918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the story starts out more originally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1501148,
    "dDurationMs": 4862,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about a young web artist from South Korea, but it quickly degenerates into nonsense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506950,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Technically speaking, the API doesn't actually let you pick a temperature bigger than 2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511170,
    "dDurationMs": 4166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's no mathematical reason for this, it's just an arbitrary constraint imposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515336,
    "dDurationMs": 4014,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep their tool from being seen generating things that are too nonsensical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519870,
    "dDurationMs": 4402,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you're curious, the way this animation is actually working is I'm taking the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524272,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20 most probable next tokens that GPT-3 generates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527011,
    "dDurationMs": 2523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seems to be the maximum they'll give me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529534,
    "dDurationMs": 3436,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then I tweak the probabilities based on an exponent of 1/5."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533130,
    "dDurationMs": 4304,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As another bit of jargon, in the same way that you might call the components of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537434,
    "dDurationMs": 4739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the output of this function probabilities, people often refer to the inputs as logits,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1542173,
    "dDurationMs": 3977,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or some people say logits, some people say logits, I'm gonna say logits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546530,
    "dDurationMs": 3887,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for instance, when you feed in some text, you have all these word embeddings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550417,
    "dDurationMs": 3543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flow through the network, and you do this final multiplication with the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1553960,
    "dDurationMs": 4281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unembedding matrix, machine learning people would refer to the components in that raw,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1558241,
    "dDurationMs": 3149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unnormalized output as the logits for the next word prediction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563330,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of the goal with this chapter was to lay the foundations for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1566697,
    "dDurationMs": 3673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understanding the attention mechanism, Karate Kid wax-on-wax-off style."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570850,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, if you have a strong intuition for word embeddings, for softmax,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1574890,
    "dDurationMs": 4316,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for how dot products measure similarity, and also the underlying premise that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1579206,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most of the calculations have to look like matrix multiplication with matrices"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583577,
    "dDurationMs": 3985,
